{title: Five Smooth Stones}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 17:1–58}
{key: C}
{tempo: 114}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [F] [C] | [G] |
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]For forty days the [F]giant [C]shouted
[G]Morning and evening, [C]loud and tall
All the soldiers [F]shook and [C]trembled
[G]No one dared to [C]fight at all
[F]Then a shepherd boy came running
[C]Bringing bread for brothers three
Said [Dm]why is everybody hiding
[G]God is bigger, come and see
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Five smooth [F]stones from the [G]stream
A sling and a shepherd's [C]bag
Not a [F]sword and not a [G]spear
But a heart that trusts in the [Am]LORD
One, two, [F]three, four, [C]five
[Dm]Little David, [G]brave and [C]wise
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [C] | [F] | [G] | [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]King Saul gave him his [F]heavy ar[C]mor
Bronze [G]helmet shining [C]on his head
David tried to [F]walk and [C]wobbled
[G]I'm not used to [C]these, he said
[F]So he took his staff and pebbles
[C]Ran to meet the giant there
[Dm]I come in the name of the LORD of [G]hosts
The God of Israel everywhere
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Five smooth [F]stones from the [G]stream
A sling and a shepherd's [C]bag
Not a [F]sword and not a [G]spear
But a heart that trusts in the [Am]LORD
One, two, [F]three, four, [C]five
[Dm]Little David, [G]brave and [C][F]wise
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [G] | [G] | [Am] | [F] |
| [G] | [G] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[F]Swing it round and [C]let it go
[G]Down the giant [Am]fell, oh [F]whoa
The [Dm]LORD does not save with [F]sword or [C]spear
When [G]you are small, God is [C]near
{end_of_bridge}

{comment: Chorus (instrumental)}
| [C] |
| [C] | [F] | [G] | [G] | ×2
| [Am] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Am]One, two, [F]three, four, [C]five
[Dm]Little David, [G]brave and [C][F]wise [G][C]
{end_of_verse}
